<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Furius Camillus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 365 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Furius Camillus was a Roman statesman and general of the early fourth century BCE. He captured the Etruscan city of Veii in 396 BCE after a long siege, and Roman tradition credited him with saving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after the Gallic sack of about 390 BCE. He was celebrated as a second founder of Rome, though much of his story is legendary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-furius-camillus.jpg" alt="Marcus Furius Camillus" width="304" height="609" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see filename or category · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Domenico_ghirlandaio,_affreschi_della_sala_dei_gigli_02_furio_camillo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
